## How to use it

The usage docs live once for every project, in the global toolset (`{{TOOLSET_DIR}}/how-to/llm-wiki/`). **The whole system on one page**: `{{TOOLSET_DIR}}/how-to/llm-wiki/user-guide.md`. **Every command**: `{{TOOLSET_DIR}}/how-to/llm-wiki/commands.md`.

**Add an external reference (article, doc, video):**
```
/wiki-update <url>
```

**Search for prior work:**
```
/wiki-search "what query"
```

**End-of-session:**
```
/wrap-up
```
Distills the session into proposed wiki entries. Stages to `_inbox/proposed/` (beside `wiki/`), then offers to promote them.

**The research cycle:**
```
/wiki-cycle
```
Gather → triage → ingest (staged for your review) → check → lint → report → commit. `--full` adds the deeper passes; `--ingest-only` and `--lint-only` narrow it.

## Need help?

**Ask the agent in plain English anytime.** The command reference (`commands.md` in the global toolset) is loaded through `CLAUDE.md`, and the agent reads the other usage pages there when a question needs them. Try:

- "What commands do I have?"
- "How do I add a URL to the wiki?"
- "Show me what's in the wiki"
- "How do I look up prior decisions?"
- "What's the difference between /wiki-update and /wiki-cycle?"

Or read the docs directly, in `{{TOOLSET_DIR}}/how-to/llm-wiki/`:

| File | When |
|---|---|
| `user-guide.md` | How the whole system works, on one page |
| `getting-started.md` | Your first hour after install |
| `commands.md` | Every command, one line each |
| `skills/wiki-update.md` | `/wiki-update` deep dive |
| `skills/wiki-cycle.md` | `/wiki-cycle` orchestrator |
| `skills/wrap-up.md` | `/wrap-up` at session end |
| `skills/wiki-search.md` | `/wiki-search` ranking |
| `drive-setup.md` | Google Drive OAuth |
| `install.md` | Installing on another machine |

The global toolset is kept by the framework's install and is never edited by hand; this wiki holds no copy of
its pages. Your project's own conventions go in `wiki/project/best-practices/`, and anything else project-specific
anywhere under `wiki/`.

## Don't

- Don't hand-edit `_MAP.md` or the `_INDEX.md` files — they're auto-generated by `wiki-map-compile.py`, `wiki-index.py` and `wiki-index-per-folder.py`
- Don't suppress contradictions in `wiki/` — both-sides-stay: keep contradictory entries cross-linked, never delete the minority view
- Don't move staged entries into `wiki/` by hand — they wait in `_inbox/proposed/` (beside `wiki/`) and `/wiki-promote` moves them

